#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:6
msgid "Function-Like Procedural Macros"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:8
msgid ""
"**Function-like procedural macros** look and feel like declarative macros to "
"the caller, but their implementation is a Rust function decorated with the "
"`#[proc_macro]` attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:17
msgid ""
"// Process input tokens and return output tokens...\n"
"    \"42\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:22
msgid "Key properties:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:24
msgid "**Declaration:** Decorated with `#[proc_macro]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:25
msgid ""
"**Function Signature:** Must accept a single `TokenStream` (the tokens "
"inside the brackets of the callsite) and return a `TokenStream`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:27
msgid ""
"**Flexible Invocation:** Like other function-like macros, callers can invoke "
"them with any kind of brackets."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:33
msgid ""
"Note that the `input` TokenStream contains only the tokens _inside_ the "
"brackets, not the macro name or the exclamation mark."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:35
msgid ""
"Emphasize that function-like procedural macros are useful when you need to "
"parse complex custom DSLs that cannot be expressed easily with declarative "
"`macro_rules!` pattern-matching."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/function-like.md:38
msgid "Mention that they may expand to expressions, statements, or items."
msgstr ""
